Build ubuntu-uefi sdcard image for raspberrypi4b:

cd ~/Downloads
wget https://cdimage.ubuntu.com/releases/25.10/release/ubuntu-25.10-desktop-arm64.iso

cd ~/build-raspberrypi4b/ubuntu-uefi

Plugin usb3 stick to PC.
sudo ./eraseusb3stick.sh
sudo mkfs.ext4 /dev/sda1
sudo fdisk -l /dev/sda
Eject usb3 stick from PC.

Plugin sdcard to PC.
sudo ./mkuefiboot.sh
sudo mkfs.vfat /dev/sda1
sudo fdisk -l /dev/sda
sudo mount /dev/sda1 /mnt
sudo 7z x ~/Downloads/RPi4_UEFI_Firmware.zip -o/mnt && sync && sudo umount /mnt
Eject sdcard from PC.

Plugin USB2 SATA ssd to PC.
sudo ./mksdcardimg.sh
sudo mkfs.vfat /dev/sda1
sudo fdisk -l /dev/sda
sudo mount /dev/sda1 /mnt
sudo 7z x ~/Downloads/ubuntu-25.10-desktop-arm64.iso -o/mnt && sync && sudo umount /mnt
Eject USB2 SATA ssd from PC.

------------------------------------------------------------------------
Install ubuntu from USB2 SATA ssd ubuntu iso to usb3 stick.
NOTE: To minimize EMI interference, put usb3 stick to rpi4b top USB3 socket,
      Put keyboard mouse to rpi4b bottom USB2 socket with USB2 extention cable.
      Put USB2 SATA ssd to rpi4b top USB2 socket.
------------------------------------------------------------------------

Plugin sdcard, usb3 stick, USB2 SATA ssd and ethernet cable to rpi4b. Power on rpi4b.
Esc -> Device Manager -> Rpi -> Advanced -> 3GB ( disable ) -> F10 -> Boot Manager -> usb flash drive.
Select install
Double click Install Ubuntu LTS icon.
Erase and install Ubuntu.
Click Install now.
Contine till finished. Restart.

Remove USB2 SATA ssd from rpi4b.
Login:
Username: linaro
Password: linaro
Disable power saving, auto suspend and screen saver.
sudo apt install net-tools openssh-server pulseaudio-utils
sudo ifconfig
uname -a
lsb_release -a
sudo dpkg-reconfigure tzdata
sudo dpkg-reconfigure locales
date
sudo apt update; sudo apt upgrade -y; sudo apt dist-upgrade -y;
sync
free
sudo shutdown -h now

Plugin usb3 stick to PC.
sudo mount /dev/sda2 /mnt
cp ./packages/firmware-brcm80211_20250410-2_all.deb /mnt/home/linaro/
sudo cp ./packages/brcmfmac43455-sdio.txt /mnt/lib/firmware/brcm/
sudo cp ./packages/BCM4345C0.hcd /mnt/lib/firmware/brcm/
sudo cp ./packages/rtlbt/* /mnt/lib/firmware/rtl_bt/
sync; sudo umount /mnt;
Eject usb3 stick from PC.

Plugin usb3 stick to rpi4b. Power on rpi4b.
uname -a
lsb_release -a
sudo dpkg -i firmware-brcm80211_20250410-2_all.deb
sync

glxinfo | grep OpenGL
date
Check if Ubuntu is running UEFI mode:
ls /sys/firmware/efi
Check display mode: ( wayland or x11 )
echo $XDG_SESSION_TYPE
Check audio driver: ( pulseaudio or pipewire )
pactl info

sudo apt install speedtest-cli python3-pip python3-setuptools rfkill

speedtest-cli --secure

aplay -l

sudo rfkill list

mainline kernel 6.17.0-6-generic cannot support rpi4b sound, GPU, wifi and bluetooth.
sudo shutdown -h now

---------------------------------------------------------------
Install vendor kernel 6.18.y
---------------------------------------------------------------

See ../kernel/README to compile vendor's kernel on PC. Then copy the resulting files to the Pi’s /boot and /lib/modules/.
Plugin usb3 stick to PC.
sudo cp -r ../kernel/linux/tmp/lib/modules/* /media/$USER/*/lib/modules
sudo cp -r ../kernel/linux/tmp/boot/* /media/$USER/*/boot
sync
Umount, Eject usb3 stick from PC.

Boot rpi4b with old kernel.
ls -la /boot
df .
sudo e2label /dev/sda2 rootfs
sudo blkid /dev/sda2   ( look for LABEL and UUID )

sudo vi /etc/grub.d/40_custom_uuid ( add
#!/bin/sh
exec tail -n +3 $0

menuentry "Boot from UUID" {
    search --no-floppy --fs-uuid --set=root --hint='usb0,gpt2' --hint='mmcblk0,gpt2' --hint='mmcblk1,gpt2' c6a25e46-e920-4b34-a543-9932b7e92395
    echo    'Loading Linux 6.18.0-rc5-v8+ ...'
    linux /boot/vmlinuz-6.18.0-rc5-v8+ root=LABEL=rootfs rootwait rw
    echo    'Loading initial ramdisk ...'
    initrd /boot/initrd.img-6.18.0-rc5-v8+
    devicetree /boot/dtb/broadcom/bcm2711-rpi-4-b.dtb
}
)

Note: change the above UUID to real UUID like: b3adbe54-ab88-4da5-a9a6-08cf87a09d69

sudo chmod +x /etc/grub.d/40_custom_uuid

sudo vi /etc/default/grub ( change GRUB_DEFAULT=0 to GRUB_DEFAULT="Boot from UUID" )
sudo update-grub  ( generate grub.cfg )
sudo update-initramfs -c -k 6.18.0-rc5-v8+
sync
sudo reboot

Remove ethernet cable from rpi4b.
Setup wifi.
sudo ifconfig
uname -a
lsb_release -a
sudo cat /sys/devices/system/cpu/cpu0/cpufreq/scaling_cur_freq
Check if Ubuntu is running UEFI mode:
ls /sys/firmware/efi

sudo apt install git zip rfkill speedtest-cli python3-pip python3-setuptools ffmpeg mpv glmark2-es2-wayland vlc vlc-plugin-video-output pavucontrol vsftpd

speedtest-cli --secure

glmark2-es2-wayland

aplay -l
pavucontrol  ( select hdmi as default )

sudo add-apt-repository ppa:mozillateam/ppa
sudo apt update
sudo apt upgrade
sudo apt install firefox-esr
firefox -> youtube.com -> search YmDNhi07_Ho

Do follows on PC, then ftp swan.mp4 to rpi4b.
(
git clone https://github.com/yt-dlp/yt-dlp.git
cd yt-dlp
make
cd ../
~/yt-dlp/yt-dlp -f 'bestvideo[ext=mp4][protocol=https]+bestaudio[ext=m4a][protocol=https]' 3qrKjywjo7Q -o swan.mp4 --postprocessor-args " -c:v libx264 -b:v 2M -c:a copy"
)

mpv --hwdec=auto-copy swan.mp4
ffplay swan.mp4
cvlc --gl=wgl --glconv=any swan.mp4

Plugin ASUS USB-BT500 bluetooth usb dongle to rpi4b.
sudo rfkill list
hciconfig hci0
hcitool dev
hciconfig -a
